Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: clear client state before stopping AP for STA reconnect

Local SL3000 fix against the pinned OpenWrt hostapd ucode extension.
mac80211 clears its stations on stop_ap, but the ucode stop/start path
retains hostapd's associated and authorized clients. After STA recovery
those clients can remain unusable until inactivity cleanup or reconnect.

Send per-client deauthentication while their keys still exist, then
clear hostapd's station state before stopping the AP. Do not change PMF,
rekeying, channel selection, or the STA reconnection state machine.

--- a/src/ap/ucode.c
+++ b/src/ap/ucode.c
@@ -590,7 +590,19 @@
 
 	for (i = 0; i < iface->num_bss; i++) {
 		struct hostapd_data *hapd = iface->bss[i];
-
+		struct sta_info *sta;
+
+		/* mac80211 stop_ap flushes its station table. Drop the matching
+		 * userspace state as well, and notify clients before their keys
+		 * are removed so that protected deauthentication is possible.
+		 */
+		if (hapd->sta_list)
+			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+				   "SL3000 AP+STA: reset clients before AP stop");
+		for (sta = hapd->sta_list; sta; sta = sta->next)
+			hostapd_drv_sta_deauth(hapd, sta->addr,
+					    WLAN_REASON_DEAUTH_LEAVING);
+		hostapd_free_stas(hapd);
 		hostapd_drv_stop_ap(hapd);
 		hapd->beacon_set_done = 0;
 	}
